01:30:36.980 --> 01:30:39.920
old sound that was

01:30:39.920 --> 01:30:41.280
called in Arabic the Daut.

01:30:41.840 --> 01:30:42.940
Called the Daut sound.

01:30:43.960 --> 01:30:44.560
We go on.

01:30:45.720 --> 01:30:47.800
The tension between inner and outer

01:30:47.800 --> 01:30:48.500
chambers

01:30:48.500 --> 01:30:51.780
is resolved

01:30:51.780 --> 01:30:53.960
in successive series of flat to star.

01:30:54.420 --> 01:30:55.940
In and out. In and out.

01:30:56.440 --> 01:30:58.140
I'm giving my lecture mechanically.

01:30:58.140 --> 01:30:59.420
What is the diktuk?

01:30:59.420 --> 01:31:02.220
Where is the dark? How are the sentences put together?

01:31:02.840 --> 01:31:04.400
All of a sudden, Borei Olam.

01:31:05.100 --> 01:31:06.040
Excuse me, Chidush.

01:31:07.660 --> 01:31:10.020
Referring to those individual grasps,

01:31:10.540 --> 01:31:11.480
lightnings flashing,

01:31:12.060 --> 01:31:15.140
that means Borei Olam is talking to us.

01:31:15.560 --> 01:31:16.440
They communicate us.

01:31:16.760 --> 01:31:17.640
My mind is continuing.

01:31:19.120 --> 01:31:21.220
He would be illuminated by flashes of lightning

01:31:21.220 --> 01:31:22.560
rapidly succeeding each other.

01:31:23.160 --> 01:31:25.220
Therefore, he would appear in continuous light

01:31:25.220 --> 01:31:26.240
with no interruption.

01:31:26.780 --> 01:31:27.540
This is Moshe Rabbein.

01:31:27.540 --> 01:31:31.100
to some others it will be flashes only once in the whole night.

01:31:31.600 --> 01:31:32.180
There are some.

01:31:32.520 --> 01:31:33.920
If there were one lightning flash for another,

01:31:34.340 --> 01:31:35.300
have long intervals.

01:31:35.660 --> 01:31:36.340
For example,

01:31:37.240 --> 01:31:39.020
Moshe Rabbenu had continuous light.

01:31:39.860 --> 01:31:41.080
Yishaya had more light.

01:31:41.880 --> 01:31:43.900
Yahaskel Ha'ben Buzig,

01:31:45.240 --> 01:31:46.400
who was Ish HaKrach,

01:31:47.060 --> 01:31:48.580
a farmer, a yokel,

01:31:49.020 --> 01:31:49.800
didn't get as well.

01:31:50.400 --> 01:31:51.540
Where do Hakhamim say this?

01:31:52.100 --> 01:31:53.500
That the Sheikha Av Hayam,

01:31:54.140 --> 01:31:56.180
when she saw Kiriat Yom Suf,

01:31:56.180 --> 01:31:57.500
because they said

01:31:57.500 --> 01:32:01.800
she's still born

01:32:01.800 --> 01:32:04.660
that's what I'm saying

01:32:04.660 --> 01:32:06.040
in other words

01:32:06.040 --> 01:32:07.440
he had a lower dimension

01:32:07.440 --> 01:32:09.640
David ha-Melekh was not a vi

01:32:09.640 --> 01:32:11.560
sometimes God talks to him but not always

01:32:11.560 --> 01:32:12.460
he talks to Natan

01:32:12.460 --> 01:32:14.760
Shom HaMelech was not a vi

01:32:14.760 --> 01:32:17.040
Daniel gets some

01:32:17.040 --> 01:32:19.520
Nevoah but he's not a vi

01:32:19.520 --> 01:32:21.820
what I learned from the

01:32:21.820 --> 01:32:23.480
Hakham here was a problem

01:32:23.480 --> 01:32:25.040
how come

01:32:25.040 --> 01:32:28.220
we say that prophecy comes to Daniel

01:32:28.220 --> 01:32:29.480
and he's not in Havim

01:32:29.480 --> 01:32:31.960
when Hakhamim put him in Ketubim

01:32:31.960 --> 01:32:33.300
and not in Nebi'im

01:32:33.300 --> 01:32:35.160
they're telling us something

01:32:35.160 --> 01:32:37.800
Hakhamim leave

01:32:37.800 --> 01:32:39.380
zero to chance

01:32:39.380 --> 01:32:41.340
the flashes

01:32:41.340 --> 01:32:43.520
of lightning

01:32:43.520 --> 01:32:45.580
represent divine inspiration

01:32:45.580 --> 01:32:46.640
from above

01:32:46.640 --> 01:32:50.240
but you can't

01:32:50.240 --> 01:32:51.360
take too much of it

01:32:51.360 --> 01:32:53.200
because too much will break you

01:32:53.200 --> 01:32:56.200
Too much of a good thing, too much sugar isn't sweet.

01:32:56.200 --> 01:32:59.200
You can't handle it. The mystics speak of

01:32:59.200 --> 01:33:02.200
Shavirat HaKalim. There's too much of the Shepa

01:33:02.200 --> 01:33:05.200
allocated, that if we absorb it, it'll break us.

01:33:05.200 --> 01:33:08.200
So sometimes in Akhtar Rahman, too much of a good thing is not good.

01:33:08.200 --> 01:33:11.200
Sometimes you don't tell everything to a child, because you're not ready for it.

01:33:11.200 --> 01:33:14.200
Ribbi Eliezer taught that the

01:33:14.200 --> 01:33:17.200
primal rite, created on the first day, would be

01:33:17.200 --> 01:33:20.200
a brilliance by which man would complicate

01:33:20.200 --> 01:33:22.060
from one end of the universe

01:33:22.060 --> 01:33:23.120
to the other.

01:33:25.320 --> 01:33:26.780
The light of the first day

01:33:26.780 --> 01:33:28.300
is not the light of nature.

01:33:28.880 --> 01:33:30.740
The light of nature was created on day four

01:33:30.740 --> 01:33:32.600
when the sun, the moon, and the stars

01:33:32.600 --> 01:33:34.460
were created. On the first day there's a

01:33:34.460 --> 01:33:35.560
different kind of light.

01:33:36.180 --> 01:33:37.820
The Hakhamim tells us the light for the

01:33:37.820 --> 01:33:38.680
Sabdi Kim and Allah Ma'an.

01:33:40.280 --> 01:33:42.480
Remember when A.V. gave that

01:33:42.480 --> 01:33:44.780
magnificent shiur four or five years ago

01:33:44.780 --> 01:33:46.960
on Yoko Tishuva chapter 8?

01:33:47.960 --> 01:33:49.760
What happens

01:33:49.760 --> 01:33:50.520
in Olam Haba,

01:33:51.120 --> 01:33:55.800
we sit and enjoy the radiance

01:33:55.800 --> 01:33:57.780
of the Zohar, the Tora,

01:33:58.220 --> 01:33:59.580
Tora's purity,

01:34:00.040 --> 01:34:01.420
brightness, brilliance

01:34:01.420 --> 01:34:02.860
of the Shekhina.

01:34:03.340 --> 01:34:05.060
Again, the metaphor of brilliance.

01:34:05.360 --> 01:34:07.220
Does that mean it's white? No.

01:34:07.580 --> 01:34:09.760
It means that's how in human

01:34:09.760 --> 01:34:10.560
language

01:34:10.560 --> 01:34:13.500
we express that experience.

01:34:13.820 --> 01:34:15.660
Just as we don't say God has a

01:34:15.660 --> 01:34:17.660
hot red nose. Only Rudolf

01:34:17.660 --> 01:34:18.420
has a red nose.

01:34:18.420 --> 01:34:21.740
You know I was going to say that?

01:34:23.700 --> 01:34:24.600
What did you say?

01:34:24.600 --> 01:34:26.780
Before I said you were thinking about it.

01:34:27.340 --> 01:34:28.020
Okay.

01:34:28.320 --> 01:34:29.660
You said you were thinking.

01:34:30.720 --> 01:34:31.200
Yes.

01:34:31.920 --> 01:34:33.340
It is not the mystical note

01:34:33.340 --> 01:34:37.420
in phenomenology and general religious experience.
